<title>USA: AccuMed acquires Difco blood culture line.</title>
<headline>AccuMed acquires Difco blood culture line.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>AccuMed International Inc, an emerging laboratory diagnostic equipment and consumable products company, said Tuesday it purchased the clinical ESP (extra sensory perception) blood culture product line from Difco Laboratories of Detroit.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>The acquisition will provide the AccuMed Microbiology division with immediate entry into the $145 million U.S. and $110 million international blood culture/mycrobacteria testing laboratory market. Difco Clinical ESP Systems sales in 1996 topped $16 million.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk  312-408-8787))</p>
